                <pb facs="0424" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3440: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-26T15:00:00-04:00">July 26, 1938—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Shanghai’s 1026, July 22, 4 p.m., and 1031, July 23, 9 p.m., in regard to
                    trains between Hankow and Canton. The Department assumes that you have brought
                    or are bringing this matter appropriately to the attention of the Chinese
                    Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
